  "findings": [
    "The candidate already sends substantially fewer browser commands; command count alone does not explain complete-flow speed.",
    "The delayed native assertion spends a median 23.12ms outside browser acknowledgements in a 24.31ms instrumented operation. Its Rust retry loop explicitly sleeps 20ms after the first miss, so resident condition detection is a supported next experiment.",
    "Fresh-context setup remains dominated by browser context/page creation, page enabling and navigation acknowledgement intervals; removing a few additional small messages will not remove those costs.",
    "Expected-failure polling differs sharply: median 76 CDP evaluations for the reference versus 2 for the candidate in these 25ms deadline operations. This is a work-count observation, not proof of a CPU or speed improvement."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Instrumentation adds a Python proxy and clock calibration; these timings do not establish production speed or resource improvements.",
    "Linux environment provisioning overlapped the diagnostic run on this shared macOS host; latency magnitudes are not isolated engine costs.",
    "Node and Python clock epochs differ on this Mac. Measured offset intervals before launch and close bound correlation uncertainty; no commands were ambiguous or outside named phases in this retained run.",
    "Acknowledgement sums can overlap. Phase unions avoid double counting, while residual phase time still includes retry/backend/lifecycle waiting and instrumentation.",
    "CDP evaluation commands do not count each predicate execution or DOM discovery visit. Resident-registry work must add those counters separately.",
    "The valid uninstrumented paired profile remains the performance evidence; the overall material-improvement and product release gates remain open."
  ],
